{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs34 reaper_ambix\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 REAPER extension adding read and write support for {\f1 \fs24 .ambix} files following the ambiX (Ambisonics eXchangeable) specification. Output can be written uncompressed (CAF container) or with WavPack lossless compression; reading auto-detects the container.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 It also adds five actions to the main action list:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b ambiX: Normalize selected item(s) to target loudness (LUFS)...}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Measures the integrated loudness of each selected item to ITU-R BS.1770 and sets the take volume so it lands on the target you enter. Ambisonic items are measured on the W channel alone; surround beds use the BS.1770-5 Annex 3 channel weighting up to 9.1.4.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b ambiX: Measure loudness of selected item(s) (LUFS)}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The same measurement, reported to the console and changing nothing, with the quietest/loudest/spread across a batch. Unlike REAPER's own item loudness analysis it knows about ambisonics.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b ambiX: Set channel count of selected track(s) and their sends...}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Sets the track channel count on every selected track and resizes the sends that carried those tracks' full width, so a whole encoder-into-bus chain changes ambisonic order in one step. Partial routings (mono sends, offset taps, hardware outputs) are left alone.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b ambiX: Convert selected item(s) to .ambix file(s)...}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Writes each selected item out as an .ambix file next to its source media, item by item rather than through the render dialog. Optional WavPack lossless compression.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b ambiX: Convert selected item(s) from FuMa to ambiX...}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Converts Furse-Malham (classic B-format) material to ACN/SN3D, per section 4.2.1 of the ambiX paper, up to third order including the reduced FuMa sets. The result can be added to the item as an extra take.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Restart REAPER after installing or updating.\par}
}

