{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs34 REAPER Live\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A touch-friendly mixer and transport for REAPER's built-in web server, meant for a phone or tablet propped next to you rather than for a desktop browser.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360\ls1\ilvl0\tx360 {\listtext\tab \bullet \tab} One strip per track plus the master: name, track colour, level meter and volume fader\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360\ls1\ilvl0\tx360 {\listtext\tab \bullet \tab} {\b Everything that can bite you starts locked.} MUTE and SOLO are hidden and the transport is inert until you open the matching padlock in the transport bar - mixer lock on the left, transport lock on the right. Each choice is remembered, and anything unexpected (a reload, a browser that refuses storage) leaves you locked rather than live\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360\ls1\ilvl0\tx360 {\listtext\tab \bullet \tab} Faders drag {\b relatively}, so putting a finger down never jumps the level to where you touched. Double-tap resets a fader to 0 dB\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360\ls1\ilvl0\tx360 {\listtext\tab \bullet \tab} Transport bar with go-to-start, stop, pause, play, record and repeat, plus the play position and time signature\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360\ls1\ilvl0\tx360 {\listtext\tab \bullet \tab} Shows a banner and dims the mixer when REAPER stops answering, so a dead connection is obvious instead of looking like a frozen desk\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Setting it up\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 ReaPack installs the page into {\f1 \fs24 reaper_www_root/}, but REAPER still has to be told to serve it:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360\ls2\ilvl0\tx360 {\listtext\tab 1.\tab} Options -> Preferences -> Control/OSC/web\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360\ls2\ilvl0\tx360 {\listtext\tab 2.\tab} Add (or edit) a {\b Web browser interface}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360\ls2\ilvl0\tx360 {\listtext\tab 3.\tab} Set a port, and choose {\f1 \fs24 reaper_mixer_live.html} as the default web browser interface page\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360\ls2\ilvl0\tx360 {\listtext\tab 4.\tab} Open {\f1 \fs24 http://<computer-ip>:<port>/} on the phone or tablet\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Both devices need to be on the same network, and REAPER has to be running.\par}
}
